<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chambéry</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chambéry is a city in the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, historic capital of Savoy, set between the Bauges and Chartreuse massifs. The counts of Savoy bought it in 1232, made it their capital in 1295 and kept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shroud-of-turin">Holy Shroud</a> in its castle chapel from 1502 until 1578. It lost its role when Emmanuel Philibert moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a> in 1563, and it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> with Savoy in 1860.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chambery.jpg" alt="Chambéry" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Florian Pépellin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chamb%C3%A9ry_-_Place_St-L%C3%A9ger.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
